// Lesson 8.4 — Boss Prototype III: Patterns & Reused Hazards
// Level 3 (Outline Only): assemble telegraphed boss attack waves and Phase 2 escalation
// by reusing TurretController, Projectile ("E_Fireball"), Platform, Spawner, and EnemyController,
// followed by a structured Self-Playtest before friend playtesting.
import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';
import { renderAskBanner } from '../../lib/walkthrough';
import { renderDecompose } from '../../lib/decompose';

const DECOMPOSE = {
  big: 'Combine reused hazards into readable boss attack waves and a Phase 2 shift, then self-playtest honestly.',
  parts: [
    {
      name: 'Reuse TurretController, Spawner, and Platform as phase-driven boss parts',
      doc: '3.1–3.4 (`TurretController.timeBetweenShots`, `"E_Fireball"`) and `Platform.isOn` in `6.3`',
      href: '6.3.html',
    },
    {
      name: 'Switch attack timings or activate extra hazards when health drops',
      doc: '8.2 (`phaseTwo` threshold inside `ChangeHealth()`) & Enemy State Machines doc',
      href: '../docs/unit-04/enemy-state-machines.html',
    },
  ],
  why:
    'A boss does not need 300 lines of custom AI math to feel tense. Mounting two `TurretController` prefabs that wake up in Phase 2, starting a moving `Platform` lift (`isOn = true`), or cutting `timeBetweenShots` in half reuses tested scripts while dramatically changing how the player moves through the arena.',
  turns: [
    'Look at `Projectile.cs` and `PlayerController.cs`: any object tagged `"E_Fireball"` deals `-2` HP on trigger enter. Why can your boss reuse `"E_Fireball"` hazard orbs or turrets right away without modifying `PlayerController`?',
    'In your self-playtest today, what is the difference between a pattern that is **hard** (fair telegraph, avoidable once learned) and a pattern that is **cheap** (unavoidable overlapping hits)?',
  ],
};

const body = `
${renderAskBanner('how do I combine reused hazards and phases into readable boss patterns?', 3)}

<p class="lead">
    Your arena stands, and the boss takes hits from both <code>E</code> and <code>Space</code>.
    Today you layer in attack patterns by reusing the hazards already inside
    <code>Assets/Scripts/</code> — then run a <strong>Self-Playtest</strong> to try beating your
    own fight before handing the controller to a friend.
</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
${renderDecompose('8.4', DECOMPOSE, 3)}

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">In the Code + Editor: Build Two Phases Out of Reused Parts (~35 min)</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~35 min</span>
    </div>

    <p>
        Pick <strong>two</strong> hazard or arena changes that trigger when your boss enters Phase 2
        (<code>health &lt;= maxHealth / 2</code>):
    </p>

    <table>
        <tr><th>Reused Tool</th><th>How to Wire It Into the Boss</th><th>How Phase 2 Changes It</th></tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>TurretController</code> + <code>Projectile</code></td>
            <td>Child turrets on the boss or corner walls tracking <code>target</code> (or fixed spawn angles) with <code>timeBetweenShots = 2.0f</code>.</td>
            <td>Drop <code>timeBetweenShots</code> to <code>1.1f</code> or call <code>SetActive(true)</code> on a second corner turret.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>EnemyController</code></td>
            <td>Boss patrols <code>patrolPoints</code> across the arena at <code>speed = 2</code>.</td>
            <td>Double <code>speed</code> to <code>4</code> or tighten aggro speed when enraged.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>Platform</code> + <code>Spawner</code></td>
            <td>Static platform at rest (<code>isOn = false</code>), or periodic wave spawn via <code>Instantiate()</code>.</td>
            <td>Flip <code>platform.isOn = true;</code> when Phase 2 starts or trigger a single minion wave via <code>Spawner</code> logic.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <div class="callout trap">
        <strong>Do NOT spawn an infinite wall of minions or bullets every frame.</strong> Calling
        <code>Instantiate()</code> inside <code>Update()</code> without checking a cooldown timer
        (<code>timer -= Time.deltaTime</code>) freezes Unity cleanly in two seconds. Guard every
        spawn with a reset timer just like <code>TurretController.cs</code> does.
    </div>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic: Combining Existing Systems</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>If a boss activates a child <code>Turret</code> in Phase 2 using <code>phaseTwoTurret.SetActive(true);</code>, why must you start that object inactive in the Scene Hierarchy — and reset it cleanly if the scene reloads?</li>
            <li><code>PlayerController.OnTriggerEnter2D()</code> subtracts <code>-2</code> HP on <code>"E_Fireball"</code>, while <code>StatManager.maxHealth</code> is <code>3</code>. How many fireballs can a player survive in one fight, and what happens if two hit in the same second?</li>
            <li>Why does giving the player a brief breather window (or resetting <code>cooldownTimer</code> cleanly between attacks) make a fight more strategic than constant random firing?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Studio Check: Self-Playtest Protocol (~25 min)</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~25 min</span>
    </div>

    <p>
        Before asking a friend to test tomorrow, try beating your own boss three times in a row
        playing <em>honestly</em> (do not walk around bugs or dodge spots only you know about):
    </p>

    <table>
        <tr><th>Run #</th><th>Style Used</th><th>Result (Win / HP Left)</th><th>Top Fairness / Timing Issue Found</th></tr>
        <tr><td>1</td><td>Melee focus (<code>KeyCode.E</code>)</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><td>2</td><td>Ranged focus (<code>KeyCode.Space</code>)</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><td>3</td><td>Mixed + double jumps + platforms</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
    </table>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic: Designing for Players Who Do Not Know Your Code</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>In your self-playtest, which strategy won way too easily (e.g., standing safely in a corner firing <code>Space</code> forever)? What single tweak closes that cheese?</li>
            <li>Compare beating your boss with melee versus ranged: did one feel useless, or did both create interesting risk/reward?</li>
            <li>Write down one visual cue you need to add tomorrow if an attack currently comes out too fast to dodge on reaction.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic: Pattern Timing</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Look at <code>timeBetweenShots</code> across all active turrets in Phase 2: if two turrets fire on identical <code>1.5f</code> timers, do they shoot in sync forever or stagger cleanly?</li>
            <li>If the player loses all health during Phase 2 and <code>StatManager.Die()</code> reloads the scene, verify every Phase 2 object starts back in Phase 1 rather than staying enraged.</li>
            <li>Name the single biggest fix from your self-playtest table that you will apply before friend playtesting next class.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="checklist">
    <h3>Checkpoint — before moving on, you must be able to:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Reuse turrets, moving platforms, spawners, or patrol speeds inside a working Phase 1 → Phase 2 fight</li>
        <li>Guard every projectile/minion spawn with a cooldown timer</li>
        <li>Self-playtest all three combat styles (melee, ranged, mixed) and log unfair spots honestly</li>
        <li>Commit and push</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <p>Need a deeper explanation? These pages cover the same concepts:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-08/index.html">Unit 8: Boss Fight</a> — attack patterns &amp; self-playtesting</li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-04/enemy-state-machines.html">Enemy State Machines</a> — patrol and aggro patterns</li>
        <li><a href="../docs/reference/unity-csharp-quickref.html">Unity + C# Quick Reference</a> — timers, <code>Instantiate()</code>, and prefabs</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Next: <a href="8.5.html">8.5 — Boss Playtest with Friends &amp; Win/Lose Loop</a> — cold playtest with classmates and close the victory/death loop.</p>
</div>`;
